    "body": "Escalation from issue-worker-high (claude-opus-5-5). Findings:\n\n1. The Ctrl + click pick operates correctly. A probe UI test made real viewport clicks (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/edge_click_modifiers.rs` harness). It did a plain click on one edge, then a Ctrl + click on a second edge (adjacent and not adjacent). The selection had 2 edges in each case, with no refusal, for these kinds:\n   - Face, Contour, Pocket, Trace, Adaptive2D, Offset2D, Engrave, Pocket3D.\n   - Orthographic and perspective camera.\n   The existing tests `contour_click_ctrl_and_shift_pick_the_same_every_time` and `pocket_click_ctrl_and_shift_pick_the_same_every_time` already pin the Ctrl add and the Ctrl toggle.\n2. The defect is in the toolpath law, not in the pick. `crates/app/src/operation/selection.rs` (`selection_geometry_in`) routes an open run as follows:\n   - Pocket, Adaptive2D, Offset2D: refusal \"is an open run - a ... cannot end mid-edge\".\n   - Trace, Engrave: refusal \"is an open run - ... machines a closed boundary\".\n   - Contour: the cutter centre rides the run. Runs that meet end to end are stitched, so the pass turns around the corner.\n   - Face: each run extends out to the stock boundary (`extend_run_to_footprint`).\n   No law reads two open edges as the walls of a region with open ends, where the pass extends past the open ends and does not turn the corner.\n3. That law is new toolpath geometry: region construction from open runs, extension past the open ends, and a gouge check against the walls. It changes the cut region. By the safety floor and the effort table, this is `effort:max`.\n\nNo code is held. The probe was not committed, and no branch was pushed. The label goes from `effort:high` to `effort:max`, and the claim is released.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
