    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T23:04:58Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/1726-first-ctrl-click · PR #1748 · pinned by pick_doors::edge_picks_that_meet_only_from_above_pass_the_pick_door, first_ctrl_click::the_first_ctrl_click_adds_the_edge_under_the_first_one, first_ctrl_click::a_plain_click_takes_an_upright_edge_and_ctrl_click_adds_to_it · merges when reviewed\n\nCause: the pick door of the pocket family refused the selection. The stitcher welds open edge runs where their ends meet when you look from above. One vertical edge, or an edge with the edge below it, becomes a ring that has no area. The door refused it, so the selection kept one edge. The list showed the stored selection correctly.\n\nReadings on `Block-w-slot` with a 2D Offset: 0 incorrect pairs of 56 in the orthographic Top view, 136 of 240 in a perspective view before the fix.\n\nThe fix: the door accepts such a stitched collapse. Generate gives the same refusal as before, and the Geometry page shows the sentence below the picks.\n\nNot exercised: a hand test in the GUI, screenshots, and a Ctrl+click with more than 4 px of pointer travel (that input starts a box selection).\n",
